Canonical at t=5 reached A-pivot 2 with **472665** terms (`res=57619667212800`) and was killed as a time bound. Canonical at t=6 completed Q-pivots then was killed before A-elim, after the t=5 swell. Those are MEASURED failures of that particular variable order at these sizes, not a refutation of the unit-pivot method.

Heuristic A-elim (same unit test) finished:

| t | A-pivots | A-elim s | terminal | bands | degrees | all tags (0,1) |
|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | 12 | 0.29 | 4×2 | 0..3 | 9..6 | yes |
| 3 | 17 | 1.44 | 6×3 | 0..5 | 13..8 | yes |
| 4 | 22 | 7.24 | 8×4 | 0..7 | 17..10 | yes |
| 5 | 27 | 24.84 | 10×5 | 0..9 | 21..12 | yes |

This is the banked pattern `2t` rows, `t` vars, bands `0..2t-1`, degrees `4t+1..2t+2`, remainder tag `(0,1)`, on **four** consecutive integers. It is MEASURED, not an all-t theorem.

Canonical at t=2..4 also ends in `2t×t` with the **same remaining names** and the **same degree multiset**, but bands are doubled in the low range (e.g. t=4: `[0,1,1,2,2,3,3,4]`) and tags are not all `(0,1)`.

Q-associate duplicates before A_t: `2t` at t=4 and t=5 (8 and 10). Auxiliaries before A-elim: `6t+2` (14,20,26,32).

Terminal polynomials (primitive over `Q[y, remaining]`, which is the degree-`<2` section of `A_t[remaining]`) are in

```text
box/k16t56-20260903/t{2,3,4}_{canonical,heuristic}_terminal.tsv
box/k16t56-20260903/t5_heuristic_terminal.tsv
```

t=5 heuristic TSV is 470698 bytes. Each row is printed as a `Q[y]` polynomial and as the `A_t` section (same section: coefficients already reduced).

## 4. Side-by-side patterns (t=2..5, MEASURED)

Verified on every completed t in `{2,3,4,5}` under heuristic, and on `{2,3,4}` under both orders unless noted.

1. Terminal size `2t × t`. Remaining names `q_{t+1}_0, q_{t+2}_1, …, q_{2t}_1`.
2. Heuristic: row of band `j` has total degree `4t+1-j` and tag `(0,1)`. Canonical: the same degrees as a **multiset**, not aligned to `j`.
3. Q-pivot coefficients follow the `q / 2q / -4q / -3q/4` spine of §1.
4. A-pivot count `5t+2`; every `Res_y(H_t, u_{t,j}) != 0`.
5. Leading coefficients (lex, remaining in the name order above), t=2,3,4 heuristic: each LC is **degree 1 in y**, of the form `N*(a y - b)` with `N in Q*`. There is **no** single polynomial in `t` that equals every LC; the linear forms change with the row. On t=2 the last two LCs contain the factor `5y-1` of `H_2` (vanishes on one split fibre; the other generators do not).
6. Lex LM always involves `q_{t+1}_0` to power 2 or 3; the next `q_{t+2}_1` carries a descending exponent along the band. Not promoted as a closed formula.
7. Resultant sequences are t-dependent integers (and a few rationals); they are **not** a single polynomial sequence independent of t. Tables: `t*_heuristic_A_pivots.tsv` and `t*_canonical_A_pivots.tsv`.

t=6 is **not** included in (1)–(2) or (5)–(6). Its Q-pivot **names**, `H_6`, and three units **are** included in (3) and the unit half of (4).

## 5. Saturation

Ring map: generators are the primitive integer associates of the terminal rows, plus `H_t` in the `Q[y, remaining]` presentation, or `minpoly=H_t` in the algebraic-extension presentation. Rabinowitsch variable `W` is a ring variable. EMPTY/NONEMPTY wrappers, actual-pair, and (on extension rings) `cbar` unit are asserted. `sat()` is not used on the terminal; `c` is already a unit and eliminated.

| t | order | modular 32003/32009/32027 | exact |
|---:|---|---|---|
| 2 | both | `[1]` each, ~0.02–0.04 s | `Q[y]+H` `std`: `[1]`, 0.02 s, 11.3 MiB |
| 3 | both | `[1]` | `A_t` `std` 0.10 s / `nfmodStd` 0.16 s, `G[1]=1` |
| 4 | both | `[1]`, ~0.1 s | `nfmodStd` 1.67 s (canonical) / 1.38 s (heuristic), 15.6 / 18.0 MiB, `G[1]=1` |
| 5 | heuristic | `[1]`, 5.61–5.69 s, ~33 MiB | `nfmodStd` **100.91 s**, 140744 KiB, input 234055 bytes, `G[1]=1` |
| 6 | — | not run | not run |

t=4 `Q[y]+H` `std` exceeded 300 s (MEASURED timeout); `nfmodStd` over `A_4` is the exact certificate, matching the charged t=4 method. t=2 minpoly is reducible, so the extension ring is not used; the product-algebra certificate is `std(H, gens)` in `Q[y,q3_0,q4_1]`.

t=5 `nfmodStd` printed `CONTROL_C_UNIT_PASS`, all RC/RK EMPTY and NONEMPTY wrappers, `MAIN_EXTRACT_RING_PASS`, `MAIN_EXACT_UNIT`, `G[1]=1`.

## 6. Controls

- **t=2,3 banked replay.** Chart dimensions, Phi, Q-pivot names and `Q*`-coefficients, `H_t`/`c_t`, grading, and (heuristic) 2t×t / bands / degrees / tags match the charged t=2 and t=3 reports. Exact `[1]` matches. Remaining **names** differ from banked `(b3,b4)` / `(b3,b4,a2_0)` because the A-pivot sequence differs; the quotient is still unit.
- **Wrapper controls.** After putting `W` in the ring: EMPTY `<u, W*u-1>=<1>` and NONEMPTY `<u-1, W*u-1> != <1>` pass on every completed Singular job used as a certificate.
- **Actual pair.** `(pi, pi-gamma^2/2)` has `J=gamma` and reciprocal-anchor degree 2, but `pi`-degrees `(1,1)`, not `(12t+4, 8t+4)`. Classifier file prints `CONTROL_ACTUAL_PAIR_PASS` and `K16_TUPLE_FAIL`. It is never a chart point.
- **t=4 generic = dedicated** by ordered tagged-equation identity.
- **Binomial identities** over `Q(t)`: pass.

## 7. FALLACY-v2

The chart is a necessary superset: unit ideal on `c != 0` proves (T) at that t; modular `[1]` is only a cross-check. `A_t` is the full rank-two algebra, a field off the split set (t=2 splits; t=5,6 do not). Raw remainders are reduced modulo `H_t` in the declared section `deg_y<2`. Variable order, coefficient field, and image checks are declared; matching names are not used as a proof. Prime marks are labels. No cv/place/series, no carrier/attainment, no exit set. Canonical swell at t=5 is reported as OPEN for that order, not filled by the heuristic analogy: heuristic `[1]` at t=5 is a **separate** exact certificate for a different (still unit) pivot sequence.

## 8. Per-t verdict

- **t=2.** CONFIRMED. Split `A_2`. Terminal 4×2. Exact `[1]`.
- **t=3.** CONFIRMED. `H_3` irreducible. Terminal 6×3. Exact `[1]`.
- **t=4.** CONFIRMED. `H_4` irreducible, `Q(√15)`. Terminal 8×4. Exact `nfmodStd` `[1]`.
- **t=5.** CONFIRMED for the heuristic (banked-pattern) spine: 10×5, bands 0..9, degrees 21..12, `nfmodStd` `[1]` in 100.91 s. Canonical A-elim OPEN (472k-term swell at step 2). `H_5` irreducible, `Q(√2)`.
- **t=6.** PARTIAL. Chart 63/93, Phi (−1,6/19), 22 Q-pivots bands 25..12, `H_6` irreducible `Q(√21)`, three units. Terminal system and saturation OPEN: after 935 s of Q-pivots the `x=1` slice conversion was still running at 45 min with no A-pivot emitted.

The uniform-in-t spine **data** from t=2..5 heuristic is the 2t×t family with remaining block `(q_{t+1}_0, q_{t+2}_1, …, q_{2t}_1)`, Q-coefficients as in §1, and A-pivot count `5t+2` with nonzero resultants. That is not a proof of the middle recurrence `u_{t,j}(y)`.

